---
import Cta from "../components/Cta.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Live from "../components/Live.astro";
import Top from "../components/Top.astro";
import { repo, version } from "../data/site";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
	title="replay demos · record and play back, live"
	description="Live demos of @voila.dev/replay: a page recorded and played back next to it, the tape op by op, masking, lost chunks and seeking. The real library, in your browser."
>
	<div class="in">
		<Top />
		<header class="phero solo"><h1>Demos</h1></header>
		<div class="pintro">
			<p>The real library, running in your browser.</p>
			<div><span class="k">Recorded</span>A small checkout page, in an iframe</div>
			<div><span class="k">Version</span>@voila.dev/replay {version}, built from this repo</div>
		</div>
	</div>

	<main class="in">
		<section id="live">
			<div class="head"><h2>Live</h2><span>The tape, op by op</span></div>
			<p class="claim lead">Click, type, switch tabs. Every change lands on a flat tape, and the copy is rebuilt from it.</p>
			<Live tape />
			<p class="note">
				A snapshot first, then a drain every 250 ms. Ops are an opcode and its operands: <code>E</code> makes an element, <code>TEXT</code> changes a
				text, <code>VAL</code> a typed value, <code>MOVE</code> and <code>TAP</code> are the pointer, <code>TICK</code> is time. The copy is a sandboxed
				iframe without scripts, built through the DOM API, never through the HTML parser.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section id="mask">
			<div class="head"><h2>Masking</h2><span>In the core, before any module</span></div>
			<p class="claim lead">Type in the card field. What you type never leaves the page.</p>
			<Live maskPicker />
			<div class="what-grid how-grid">
				<div><span class="k">inputs (default)</span>Typed values become six stars, whatever their length: not even the length leaves. The page's own text stays readable.</div>
				<div><span class="k">text</span>All text too. Only the layout and the pointer are left.</div>
				<div><span class="k">Always</span>Passwords, card numbers, one-time codes and hidden fields, whatever the mode. Here, the card field is <code>cc-number</code>.</div>
			</div>
			<p class="note">Per element: <code>data-va-mask</code>, <code>data-va-unmask</code>, <code>data-va-block</code> (an empty box of the same size).</p>
		</section>

		<section id="holes">
			<div class="head"><h2>Holes</h2><span>Said, not replayed</span></div>
			<p class="claim lead">Networks lose things. A replay that does not say so shows a page that never existed.</p>
			<Live drop />
			<p class="note">
				Each chunk carries its rank and the number its first node takes. When one is missing, the player marks a hole and waits for the next
				snapshot, rather than apply changes to nodes it never received. Here the recorder takes a new snapshot 2 s after the loss; in production
				<code>connect</code> asks for one when the server says so.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section id="seek">
			<div class="head"><h2>Seek</h2><span>From the nearest checkpoint</span></div>
			<p class="claim lead">Seeking back does not replay from the start.</p>
			<Live seek />
			<p class="note">
				Every 10 s of tape, the player keeps a checkpoint: a copy of the rebuilt page, its node numbers, and what a copy does not carry (constructed
				sheets, canvas pixels, modal dialogs and popovers, scroll positions, frames). A seek starts from the nearest checkpoint or snapshot before it.
				Past 64 checkpoints, one in two goes.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section id="source">
			<div class="head"><h2>Source</h2><span>What runs on this page</span></div>
			<div class="arch-grid code-grid">
				<pre class="code"><span class="c">// the recorded page lives in an iframe</span>
const rec = record(frame.contentWindow, {"{"} mask, modules: [cssom()] {"}"});
const snap = rec.snap();
const player = createPlayer({"{"}
  root: stage,
  chunks: [{"{"} base: snap.base, seq: 0, tape: snap.tape {"}"}],
{"}"});

setInterval(() =&gt; {"{"}
  const d = rec.drain();
  player.append([{"{"} base: d.base, seq: ++seq, tape: d.tape {"}"}]);
  if (!player.playing) player.play();
{"}"}, 250);</pre>
				<div>
					<p class="note">
						No server here: chunks go straight from the recorder to the player. In production, <code>connect</code> sends them to your endpoint,
						gzipped where the browser can, with long strings and snapshot pieces by hash.
					</p>
					<p class="note"><a href={repo}>Code on GitHub ↗</a></p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<Cta />
	</main>
	<div class="in"><Footer /></div>
</Base>
